      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "Action Plan public hearing and adoption May 19, 2026 for PY 2026-27; HOME development funds are awarded through the January to March Affordable Housing Development NOFO. A new three-year Urban County Joint Powers Agreement for July 1, 2027 to June 30, 2030 was approved August 11, 2026 with Fowler, Kerman, Kingsburg, Mendota, Reedley and Selma committed, Sanger and Parlier deciding in August 2026, and Orange Cove leaving the JPA.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Fresno County splits housing work three ways: the Department of Public Works and Planning, Community Development Division (ComDev) runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA and the annual Affordable Housing Development NOFO; the County Administrative Office's new Office of Housing and Homelessness (OHH, created November 18, 2025) administers HHAP, the Continuum of Care and Transitional Rent and is absorbing housing programs from Behavioral Health and ComDev (Phase 2 approved November 3, 2026); and the Department of Behavioral Health co-applies for Homekey+ and NPLH and funds BHSA housing. Fresno Housing (the joint City and County Housing Authorities) is the dominant developer and voucher source. The City of Fresno and Clovis are separate entitlements with their own programs (Pass 3). fresnocountyca.gov and fresnohousing.org open normally; Board records are on fresnocounty.legistar.com and the Legistar web API client 'fresnocounty'. HOME is the base of every County capital commitment; the County banks match and carries over unspent HOME, which is why the 2026-27 development line ($5.3 million) is several times the annual allocation. Reservations in the 2026-27 plan: Reedley Elderly $2,000,000, Selma Elderly $2,000,000, Sendero Commons $2,950,000 (HOME-ARP $2,500,000 development plus $450,000 operating, alongside PLHA $2,364,219), Park Kingsburg $2,000,000, HOME-ARP supportive services $772,651 and nonprofit operating and capacity $495,200. CDBG is not used for housing development. Source is the May 19, 2026 Board item (file 26-0444) with the Annual Action Plan attachment.",
